1
00:00:00,920 --> 00:00:04,080
我是杰森.西弗，是个心理医生
Hi, I'm Jason Seaver. I'm a psychiatrist.

2
00:00:04,460 --> 00:00:05,000
过去15年里 我致力于解决患者的问题
I've spent the last 15 years helping people with their problems.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,307
fitbbs chengse

4
00:00:07,307 --> 00:00:08,672
我是麦姬.西弗
And I'm Maggie Seaver.

5
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:10,900
过去15年里，我一直围着孩子们转
I've spent the last 15 years helping our kids...

6
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:13,100
解决那些杰森也束手无策的问题
with problems even Jason wouldn't believe.

7
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:16,860
现在麦姬已重操旧业 在一家当地报社做记者
Now Maggie has gone back to work as a reporter for the local newspaper.

8
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:19,140
杰森把他的诊所搬到了家里
And Jason has moved his practice into the house...

9
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:20,480
这样就可以陪着孩子们了
so he could be there for the kids.

10
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:22,600
-他们是可爱的孩子 -大多时候都是
- They're great kids. - Most of the time.

11
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:24,000
但是有时…
And the rest of the time...

12
00:00:24,591 --> 00:00:27,116
-反正你会喜欢他们的 -没错
- You'll love them anyway. - Yeah.

13
00:00:27,594 --> 00:00:28,720
鬼才相信
Unbelievable.

14
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:38,000
(English Subtitle) Growing.Pains.S01E01 -= Pilot =- Subripped by zerox

15
00:01:22,740 --> 00:01:25,520
夫人，放下锅铲 否则就搅你一下
All right, lady, drop that spatula or you're scrambled.

16
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:28,920
尽管放马过来
Go ahead. Make my day.

17
00:01:37,230 --> 00:01:38,219
Well...

18
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:39,920
好像是我在搅你哦
I guess I showed you.

19
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:42,880
再搅一下
Show me more.

20
00:01:43,503 --> 00:01:45,562
杰森，孩子们都在呢
Jason, the kids.

21
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:48,840
等下再亲他们
I can kiss the kids later.

22
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:54,280
我看过一篇文章 说夫妻都工作的家庭…
You know, I read an article that said that two-career couples...

23
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:58,000
尤其要注意保持…
should really make special effort to always remain...

24
00:01:58,985 --> 00:02:00,145
活泼
frisky.

25
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:02,920
早饭的时候？
At breakfast?

26
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:05,100
早中晚饭
At all meals.

27
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:11,460
怎么，你们不会亲腻的吗？
What's the matter, you guys aren't getting enough?

28
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:16,500
麦克，小孩的这种言行 可是会挨揍的哦
Mike, a lot of kids would get smacked for a remark like that.

29
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:19,600
得了吧，老爸，你不能打我 你可是自由人道主义者
Come on, Dad, you can't hit me. You're a liberal humanist.

30
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:21,660
不包括意外情况
Could be an accident.

31
00:02:23,476 --> 00:02:25,410
我真是求之不得
It could be a dream come true.

32
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:28,100
妈妈，我们干脆把凯罗卖掉 换台车载音响吧？
Mom, can't we sell Carol and get a tape deck for the Volvo?

33
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:31,280
麦克，你重新诠释了“草包”这个词
Mike, you give new meaning to the word "vacuous."

34
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:35,060
是吗？那它原来的意思是啥？
Oh, yeah? What was the old meaning?

35
00:02:37,190 --> 00:02:38,714
懒得跟你说了
I rest my case.

36
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:42,740
本…
Ben. Ben.

37
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:47,080
什么这么好笑呢？
What's so funny, Ben?

38
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:51,160
菲莉丝.乔治又说错话了! [早间新闻主播]
That Phyllis George! She screwed up again!

39
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:56,065
宝贝，你在看什么呢？
Honey, what's that you're reading about?

40
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:59,040
这上面说，当宇宙膨胀时…
It says here that as the universe expands...

41
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:04,140
一切物质都会变得越来越老化和混沌
all matter is slowly degenerating into a state of total disorganization.

42
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:07,820
感谢上帝，我以为只有我才这样
Thank God. I thought it was just me.

43
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,540
你们晚上有啥节目？
Yeah, so, what are you guys doing tonight?

44
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:14,840
“汗之屋”？太棒了!
The House of Sweat? Yeah, great!

45
00:03:18,660 --> 00:03:22,420
我迟点再打给你 好，拜
Hey, look, can I talk to you guys later? Yeah. Bye.

46
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:26,940
麦克，“汗之屋”是什么意思？
Mike, what is "The House of Sweat"?

47
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:30,020
就是…
Well... It's, you know...

48
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:33,200
高速公路旁新开的一家 未成年人舞厅
It's that new under-20 dance club on Jericho Turnpike.

49
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:35,800
听这名字挺不错的，老妈
Yeah, and it sounds like a great idea, Mom.

50
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:39,840
那是个安全，健康的 年轻人聚会场所
It's a safe, wholesome place for teens to congregate.

51
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:43,740
人聚得越多，脑子就越小
And the larger the group, the smaller their brains get.

52
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:46,080
别这样嘛，麦姬…
Come on, Maggie...

53
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,180
是啊，别这样嘛
Yeah, come on, Maggie.

54
00:03:50,820 --> 00:03:52,880
对了，我该出去等校巴了
Yes. Well, time to go wait for that school bus.

55
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,760
动作快点的话没准还能在 无烟区抢到座位
You know, if I hurry, I can still get a seat in the non-smoking section.

56
00:03:58,104 --> 00:04:00,538
-再见，宝贝 -妈妈再见
- Bye, sweetie. - Bye, Mom.

57
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:02,380
再见，本，我爱你
Bye, Ben. I love you.

58
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:06,760
再见，本
Later, Ben.

59
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:12,600
9点上班前 我还有点案头工作要做
I still have some paperwork to do before my 9:00 gets here.

60
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:18,960
如果你刚才意犹未尽 而且有丁点空闲的话…
And if you start feeling frisky and you have eight or 10 seconds before work...

61
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:21,640
你知道去哪找我
you know where to find me.

62
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:29,100
本，怎么还没走？ 你会误了校车的
Ben, what are you doing here? You'll miss the bus.

63
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:34,900
怎么了，宝贝？
What's the matter, honey?

64
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:37,460
爸爸没把我的胳膊肘治好
Dad didn't know how to do my elbow.

65
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:40,960
让我看看
Let me see.

66
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:48,620
爸爸做得很好 他给你贴了个超人创可贴
Dad did a great job on this cut. Superman Band-Aids, the works.

67
00:04:51,340 --> 00:04:54,060
我明白了，他没有亲亲
I get it. He didn't kiss it.

68
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:59,080
没说“我爱你，小南瓜头”
And say, "I love you, little pumpkin head."

69
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:02,120
太不投入了
It was all so clinical.

70
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:09,200
妈妈，你非要回去工作吗？
Mom, how come you had to go back to work?

71
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:14,120
不是非去不可，是我想去
I didn't have to, Ben. I wanted to.

72
00:05:15,780 --> 00:05:16,720
过来
Come here.

73
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:22,360
本，假如你在一所房子里…
Ben, imagine you had to spend...

74
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:25,420
闷了15年，哪也不准去
15 years in this house without ever going out to play.

75
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,260
你也会疯的，对吗？
You'd go crazy, wouldn't you?

76
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:32,460
不管你信不信 很多大人对工作也是这种态度
Well, believe it or not, a lot of grown-ups feel the same way about work.

77
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:34,793
是够惨的，妈妈
That's sick, Mom.

78
00:05:36,569 --> 00:05:39,663
我知道这对我们大家都有影响
Ben, I know this has been a big change for all of us.

79
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:44,300
而且我对你也放不下心 因为你最小
And I worry about not being here for you, because, well, you're the youngest.

80
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:47,320
我对凯罗放不下心是因为…
And I worry about not being here for Carol...

81
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:49,420
她是女孩，女孩需要妈妈
because she's a girl and she needs her mother.

82
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:52,440
我不放心麦克是因为…
And I worry about not being here for Mike...

83
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:54,960
我怕他老是闯祸
to keep him from accidentally blowing something up.

84
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:58,520
而且，我对爸爸也放心不下…
And, believe me, I worry about leaving your father here...

85
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:00,480
因为他要应付你们三个小魔怪
to cope with all you monsters.

86
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:05,540
不要担心，妈妈 你这样会发疯的
You shouldn't worry so much, Mom. You'll make yourself crazy.

87
00:06:07,367 --> 00:06:09,699
我爱你，小南瓜头
I love you, little pumpkin head.

88
00:06:14,780 --> 00:06:16,560
我总是做同一个梦，大夫
It's always the same dream, Doc.

89
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:23,440
我在地铁里 一个女人坐在我对面
I'm on a subway and this woman sits across from me.

90
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:25,460
她长得很漂亮
This beautiful woman.

91
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:30,590
我看着她，她看着我
And I look at her. She looks at me.

92
00:06:32,260 --> 00:06:33,740
我舔舔嘴
I lick my lips.

93
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:38,240
她也舔舔嘴
She licks her lips.

94
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:40,680
就这么舔下去
This goes on.

95
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:45,060
最后她凑过来，低声对我说…
Then, finally, she leans across, and she whispers to me:

96
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:49,660
“你的膝盖好大”
"You have huge knees."

97
00:06:52,710 --> 00:06:54,240
这话啥意思呢，大夫？
Does that mean anything, Doc?

98
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:03,840
每人5块钱对口费
That should be good for about $5 apiece.

99
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:08,000
就到这里，沃特
Good visit, Walter.

100
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:10,820
别太过担心了，好吗？
And don't worry too much about this thing. Okay?

101
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:23,520
下周见，再见
See you next week. Bye-bye.

102
00:07:25,178 --> 00:07:27,806
-爸，能跟你说句话吗？ -没问题
- Could I talk to you for a second, Dad? - Sure.

103
00:07:28,140 --> 00:07:31,020
-到你办公室说 -好的
- In your office. - Sure.

104
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:46,140
-小孩子 -我吗？
- Kids. - Me?

105
00:07:46,432 --> 00:07:47,421
对
Yeah.

106
00:07:49,860 --> 00:07:52,940
你想跟我谈什么呢？
So you wanted to talk about something?

107
00:07:54,106 --> 00:07:55,664
是的
Yeah.

108
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:59,340
最主要的是 向你表示这里一切安好
Mostly I just wanted to mention how smoothly things have been running...

109
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:03,060
自从你妻子回去上班 你在家里接待患者
since the wife went back to work and you moved your practice into the house.

110
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:04,680
谢谢
Well, thank you.

111
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:08,660
爸，我们一直都是朋友关系，对吧？
Dad, we've been friends now for a long time, right?

112
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:10,460
断断续续吧
Off and on, yeah.

113
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:12,440
断断续续，我喜欢这样
"Off and on." I love that.

114
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:16,420
老爸，还记得我今早说过的 那个舞厅吧？
See, Dad, you know that dance hall place that I mentioned this morning?

115
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:17,720
汗之屋？
The House of Sweat?

116
00:08:18,064 --> 00:08:19,053
是的
Yeah.

117
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:22,180
杰里和我商量了一下，我们决定…
Jerry and I were talking and we decided...

118
00:08:22,201 --> 00:08:23,259
杰里？
Jerry?

119
00:08:23,936 --> 00:08:25,426
对，杰里.德利什
Yeah, Jerry Dellish.

120
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:27,820
他是我的老朋友，车技一流
He's an older friend of mine. Excellent driver...

121
00:08:27,820 --> 00:08:29,400
学过两年驾驶
with two years of driver's ed.

122
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:31,400
学过两年驾驶？
Two years of driver's ed?

123
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:35,500
是的，第一节课时他撞上了一条狗
Yeah. See, in his first class he ran over a dog.

124
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:37,760
不过打那以后，他车开得很棒
But he drove beautifully after that.

125
00:08:38,384 --> 00:08:41,979
那只是只微不足道的鲁莽小狗
We're talking about one tiny, reckless little dog here, Dad.

126
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,920
-算它倒霉 -是啊
- Tough break. - Yeah.

127
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:47,280
总之，我们想今晚去那里玩会儿
So, anyway, I was thinking that maybe we could go down there tonight.

128
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:49,020
杰里开车，所以不用你接送
Jerry would drive so you wouldn't have to do...

129
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:50,120
你老妈会怎么说？
What would your mother say?

130
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:52,186
妈妈？
Mom?

131
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:56,120
我想她会说…
I guess she would say...

132
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,660
那个词应该怎么说来着？
What's the phrase I'm looking for here, Dad?

133
00:08:59,672 --> 00:09:01,572
-没门 -是的，就这个
- "No"? - Yeah, that's it.

134
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:04,060
我想我是去不了的了，是吗？
I guess that means I can't go, right?

135
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:07,580
我只是不想你每次跟我套近乎…
Well, it just means I don't like you coming in here...

136
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:08,920
都是带有目的
and trying to get away with something.

137
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:11,760
我不希望我们的关系变成这样
That's not the relationship I want to have with you.

138
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:13,920
对不起，爸爸
I'm sorry, Dad.

139
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:15,760
好吧，听我说
All right, now, look.

140
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:18,820
现在家里我说了算 我们可按我的方针办事
Now that I'm in charge at home, we can try things my way.

141
00:09:18,820 --> 00:09:20,020
太棒了!
All right!

142
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:23,480
你还不知道我的方针是啥呢
You don't even know what my way is.

143
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:25,760
当然知道，更多的自由
Sure I do, Dad. It's a Sinatra song.

144
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:29,860
你的领悟能力真强，麦克
You're walking a fine line here, Mike.

145
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:32,480
好吧，我们得作个约定
Okay, look, here's the deal.

146
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:35,620
我会给你更多的自由
I'll give you a little more freedom.

147
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:38,800
但你也要保证承担更多的责任
You've got to promise me a lot more responsibility.

148
00:09:39,380 --> 00:09:42,700
没问题，老爸 我发誓，我可以全面承担责任
Hey, no problem, Dad. I swear, I am ready for total responsibility.

149
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:45,440
麦克，连我都不敢说全面承担责任
Mike, I'm not ready for total responsibility.

150
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:47,500
你说得对，对不起
You're right. Sorry.

151
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:50,500
好了，那你玩得开心点吧
Okay. You go out and have a good time.

152
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:52,780
记住我们刚才说的话
Just remember what we talked about.

153
00:09:52,980 --> 00:09:54,640
绝对记住，谢谢爸爸 我保证
Absolutely, Dad! Thanks, I promise.

154
00:09:58,360 --> 00:10:00,320
对了，妈妈咋办？ 她要是发火咋办？
Wait. What about Mom? What if she's mad?

155
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:04,720
麦克，你妈又不是魔王 我跟她说，她会通情达理的
Mike, your mom's not an ogre. I'll talk to her. She'll understand.

156
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:06,800
你让他什么？
You let him do what?

157
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:10,540
麦姬，他都15岁了
Maggie, he's 15 years old now.

158
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:11,620
15岁又怎样？
So he's 15.

159
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:13,640
这简直毫无道理
It's completely arbitrary...

160
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:16,400
随便找个年纪划分孩子的成熟兴否
to just pick an age like that and say that's when a kid is mature.

161
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:20,200
莫扎特15岁时便写了七部交响乐
You know, by the time Mozart was 15, he'd written seven symphonies.

162
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:24,040
那是因为莫扎特的父亲 没让他去“汗之屋”
That's because Mozart's father didn't let him go to The House of Sweat.

163
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:28,540
他和谁一起去？
Who did he go with?

164
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:31,080
不知道，好像一个叫杰里.德利什的
I don't know, some kid. Jerry Dillish, Dellish.

165
00:10:31,831 --> 00:10:34,561
杀狗大王德利什？
Jerry "Dog-Killer" Dellish?

166
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:39,500
麦姬，他不过是撞了只狗狗而已
Maggie, he hit one dog.

167
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:43,560
可他来回撞了四次
Yeah, but he hit it four times.

168
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:47,620
好吧…
Okay, well...

169
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:50,160
麦克又不是杰里
Mike isn't Jerry.

170
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:53,580
而且孩子需要一定的自由 来培养责任感
And a kid needs some freedom in order to learn responsibility.

171
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:59,080
杰森，我知道你信奉“人类潜力无限”
Jason, I know you believe in this "unlimited human potential"...

172
00:10:59,558 --> 00:11:00,582
这种废话
stuff.

173
00:11:00,820 --> 00:11:02,320
这句话对你的患者也许适用
And that's great for your patients.

174
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:04,480
-但要是用在… -我们的孩子
- But when it comes... - To our own children...

175
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:06,100
-我相信人都有… -原罪
...I believe in original... - Sin.

176
00:11:06,632 --> 00:11:07,690
原罪
Sin.

177
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:12,400
也许我真不该回去上班
I don't know. Maybe I shouldn't have gone back to work.

178
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:14,960
行了，麦姬，别这么说
Now, come on, Maggie, don't say that.

179
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:19,960
你花了15年时间建立个家庭 你理应得到上班的奖励
You took 15 years off to raise a family, and you deserve to go back to work now.

180
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:23,120
但你该给我和孩子们多点信任
You just have to have a little more faith in me and the kids.

181
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:27,240
也许你说得对
Maybe you're right.

182
00:11:27,920 --> 00:11:28,880
这还用说
Of course I'm right.

183
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:33,340
我们不该担心，而是应该庆祝…
We shouldn't be worrying, we should be celebrating...

184
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:38,720
所以，请恕小生冒昧 现已将一瓶冰镇香槟…
which is why I've taken the liberty of placing some chilled champagne...

185
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:40,540
置于床边小桶
in a little bucket beside the bed.

186
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:43,640
还在床上铺好了一张缎子床单
Slipped some satin sheets on the old bouncer.

187
00:11:45,760 --> 00:11:47,960
缎子床单？你？
Satin sheets? You?

188
00:11:48,541 --> 00:11:49,599
是的
Yeah.

189
00:11:50,820 --> 00:11:53,440
店里的营业员还给我看了一对夫妇…
The guy in the store showed me some "before" and "after" pictures...

190
00:11:53,440 --> 00:11:54,760
睡这张床单前后的照片
of a couple who tried them.

191
00:11:57,040 --> 00:11:58,380
他们看上去很满足
They looked very satisfied.

192
00:12:00,240 --> 00:12:02,500
本和凯罗咋办？
What about Ben and Carol?

193
00:12:02,940 --> 00:12:05,780
我在他们的汽水里下了点安眠药
Well, I slipped some sleeping pills into their Gatorade.

194
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:08,600
他们会睡上3个星期
They'll be asleep for about three weeks.

195
00:12:09,161 --> 00:12:09,500
杰森!
Jason!

196
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:14,480
我没有真放，不过他们的确眯了 我们可以…
Well, I didn't really. But they are... And we can...

197
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:23,200
你好，对，我是杰森.西弗
Hello? Yeah, this is Jason Seaver.

198
00:12:24,780 --> 00:12:28,260
不，你一定找错人了 你先去脱衣服
No, you must be looking for someone else. Take your clothes off.

199
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:33,420
不会的，我家的麦克才15岁 开车的应该不是他
No, our Mike is only 15, so he wouldn't be driving a car.

200
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:37,900
明白了
I see.

201
00:12:41,140 --> 00:12:42,220
他说什么？
What did he say?

202
00:12:42,780 --> 00:12:45,500
他说“所以你家麦克才会在我们监狱里”
He said, "That's why your Mike is in our jail."

203
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:04,660
你犯啥事了，小鬼？
What are you in for, kid?

204
00:13:05,084 --> 00:13:06,244
我…
I...

205
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:08,880
我杀人，想看他怎么挂掉
I killed a man just to watch him die.

206
00:13:13,025 --> 00:13:14,083
你呢？
You?

207
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:16,360
没付停车费
Unpaid parking tickets.

208
00:13:17,163 --> 00:13:18,926
糟了，我妈来了!
Oh, no, it's my mom!

209
00:13:18,980 --> 00:13:21,780
别激动，麦姬 还不知道实际情况哪
Come on, Maggie, we don't even know the facts yet.

210
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:24,980
我是说，和警察较点小劲…
I mean, it's not so unusual for a teenage boy...

211
00:13:24,980 --> 00:13:26,620
在青少年里并不那么少见
to have a minor run-in with the police.

212
00:13:27,580 --> 00:13:29,600
有些警察本身就够横的
Some of these guys can be real macho head-bangers.

213
00:13:31,340 --> 00:13:34,900
嗨，要不要来杯热可可？ 我刚弄了一壶
Hiya, you folks care for some hot cocoa? I just made a fresh pot.

214
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:38,800
我们是西弗夫妇 你们关了我们儿子
Look, we're the Seavers. You've locked up our son.

215
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:41,440
一位警官声称他在开车
An officer claimed he was driving a car.

216
00:13:42,260 --> 00:13:42,840
是的，先生
Yes, sir.

217
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:46,100
我们是在“汗之屋”的停车场捉到他的
We picked him up in The House of Sweat parking lot.

218
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:49,780
他开着车转了12分钟的圈
He'd been driving in circles for approximately 12 minutes.

219
00:13:50,480 --> 00:13:55,120
一个15岁的孩子 拿朋友的车过一下手瘾
Okay, so a 15-year-old boy drives his friend's car around the lot a few times.

220
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:58,720
我有没说到他还刮花了一辆警车？
Did I mention he sideswiped a police car on the way out?

221
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:00,180
他什么？
He what?

222
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:02,880
他像剥橘子一样 把保险杠给掀掉了
He tore that bumper off like he was peeling an orange.

223
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:06,660
值350美圆的橘子
A $350 orange.

224
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:17,680
嗨，爸妈，你们起色不错嘛
Hiya, Dad, Mom. You look good tonight.

225
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:21,220
你看起来年轻多了
You look young.

226
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:24,020
出来吧，儿子
Come on, son.

227
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:26,600
妈，爸，这位是杰里
Mom, Dad, this is Jerry.

228
00:14:30,680 --> 00:14:33,840
这种情形是挺难看出我俩的友情
I guess it's kind of hard to see the basis of our friendship, huh?

229
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:40,360
我只知道，他有种旁若无人的气质
I don't know. He has a certain carefree charm.

230
00:14:41,513 --> 00:14:43,344
你应该看看他清醒时的样子
You should see him when he's sober.

231
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:46,840
麦克，罚你两个月不准出门
Mike, you will be grounded for two months.

232
00:14:47,620 --> 00:14:48,380
两个月？
Two months?

233
00:14:49,340 --> 00:14:52,260
-爸，快跟妈讲讲道理啊？ -讲过了，麦克
- Dad, can't you talk to her? - Oh, I did, Mike.

234
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:54,140
本来只要一个月的
Originally, it was one month.

235
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:56,487
这么说你加了一个月
Dad, that means you added a month.

236
00:14:56,660 --> 00:14:58,720
这下没辙了吧？
Nothing gets by you, does it?

237
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:01,900
爸，你说你会跟她说…
Dad, you said you'd talk to her...

238
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:03,760
该死，麦克 你说你会负起责任的!
Damn it, Mike, you said you could act responsibly!

239
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:06,080
我现在不想再听到你唧唧歪歪，明白？
Now I don't want to hear another word out of you! Is that clear?

240
00:15:34,133 --> 00:15:35,122
哇哦
- Whoa. - Whoa.

241
00:15:42,340 --> 00:15:46,260
真是个浪漫的夜晚
Oh, yeah, our romantic evening.

242
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:52,360
看来没用过缎子床单的人真可能会…
Anyone who's not used to satin sheets could easily have an accident...

243
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:54,080
麦姬，别跟我说教了
Maggie, don't patronize me. Okay?

244
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:59,060
我那该死的睡衣在哪？
And where the hell are my pajamas?

245
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:03,300
对不起，我也不大确定在哪
Gee, I'm sorry. I'm really not sure.

246
00:16:03,562 --> 00:16:06,429
你是不是觉得我连一套…
You wouldn't think it'd be so damn tough to keep tabs...

247
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:08,460
睡衣睡裤都管教不好？
on a pair of pajamas around here.

248
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:10,760
杰森，我不明白你为啥这么生气
Jason, I don't understand why you're so upset.

249
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:13,880
他又不是第一次闯祸了
I mean, it's not like this is the first time he's screwed up.

250
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:14,960
谁闯祸了？
Who screwed up?

251
00:16:15,674 --> 00:16:16,766
麦克啊
Mike.

252
00:16:16,780 --> 00:16:21,000
谁说麦克了？ 我生气是因为找不到睡衣
Who said anything about Mike? I'm upset because I can't find my pajamas.

253
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:23,900
我只不过一时没盯住自己的睡衣…
I mean, if you just left a pair of pajamas around...

254
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:25,985
转眼间这么一大件睡衣…
and these are big pajamas I'm talking about...

255
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:29,580
就这么人间蒸发掉了
And to think that they just vanished into thin air...

256
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:31,480
这能不让人恼火吗？
Well, wouldn't you be pretty upset?

257
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:38,020
的确也是，不过话说回来 我倒很喜欢你生气时的样子
Absolutely. In fact, I'm amazed at the way you're holding together.

258
00:16:46,372 --> 00:16:47,464
怎么了？
What?

259
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:53,840
我从没见过爸爸气到不想说话的
I've never seen Dad actually too mad to talk.

260
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:59,180
多谢你的支持 我感觉自己已经洗心革面了
Thanks for your support. You know, I feel like a new man now.

261
00:16:59,284 --> 00:17:00,649
对不起
I'm sorry.

262
00:17:01,380 --> 00:17:02,900
其实也没那么糟啦
Look, it's not so bad.

263
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:06,420
没准过了一年后 他回想起这件事时还会笑呢
I bet, in a year, he'll look back at this whole thing and laugh.

264
00:17:09,660 --> 00:17:10,820
也许是暗地里笑
Okay, maybe chuckle.

265
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:15,720
好吧，我承认
Okay, I admit it.

266
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:23,400
我生气是因为麦克
I'm upset with Mike.

267
00:17:26,311 --> 00:17:27,300
Oh?

268
00:17:27,840 --> 00:17:28,440
你不气吗？
Aren't you?

269
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:31,180
当然，我气炸了
Absolutely. I'm furious.

270
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:35,240
不过我对他以前干的几件事更生气
But no more furious than I've been at him a dozen other times before.

271
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:39,060
他还是个孩子 你还能要求他怎样？
I mean, he's a kid, Jason. What did you expect?

272
00:17:39,580 --> 00:17:42,300
可他曾坐在我跟前信誓旦旦说…
Yeah, but he sat not 3 feet away from me and he said:

273
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:45,040
“爸，我发誓，我会全面负起责任”
"Dad, I swear it, I'm ready for total responsibility."

274
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:50,240
杰森，连你都不能负起全部责任
Jason, you are not ready for total responsibility.

275
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:53,360
面对现实吧，这孩子15岁了
I mean, face it, the boy is 15.

276
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:57,520
他是荷尔蒙驱动的闯祸机器
He's a hormone with feet.

277
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:04,620
我知道，但总有一天 他会长大成人的
I know, but someday that hormone will be a man.

278
00:18:05,140 --> 00:18:08,160
我希望他到时能有点责任感
And I want that man to have a sense of responsibility.

279
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,420
去跟他谈谈
Go talk to him.

280
00:18:13,125 --> 00:18:15,093
不谈你是睡不着的了
You won't sleep if you don't.

281
00:18:16,980 --> 00:18:23,340
别担心，我会继续寻找睡衣
Don't worry. I'll continue the search for the pajamas.

282
00:18:40,986 --> 00:18:41,975
干嘛？
What?

283
00:18:42,354 --> 00:18:43,821
你睡着了
You were asleep.

284
00:18:44,523 --> 00:18:48,050
睡着了？是睡着了
I was? I was.

285
00:18:48,193 --> 00:18:49,524
这么说那只是场梦
And it was a dream.

286
00:18:55,234 --> 00:18:56,599
你还在生气？
You're still angry?

287
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:04,500
爸，我知道这不是理由 但杰里的车确实很难控制
Hey, Dad, I know this is no excuse, but Jerry's car handles really badly.

288
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:10,580
我是看到杰里有点喝醉后 才不让他开车的
And I was the one who decided Jerry was too drunk to drive.

289
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,700
麦克，他醉到不省人事
Mike, he was unconscious.

290
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:16,480
我知道
I know.

291
00:19:17,180 --> 00:19:19,600
你看到他醉成那样时 你应该怎么做？
What are you doing with a kid who drinks like that?

292
00:19:20,692 --> 00:19:22,125
应该给你电话
I should've called you.

293
00:19:22,380 --> 00:19:22,940
那为啥没打？
Why didn't you?

294
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:27,840
爸，那里有很多女孩…
Well, Dad, there was these girls there...

295
00:19:28,460 --> 00:19:31,720
当然，不希望她们知道你有家长
Of course. Wouldn't want them to think you had parents.

296
00:19:34,060 --> 00:19:37,660
麦克，如果我不能信任你 你觉得我们的关系会走向何方？
Mike, what kind of a relationship are we going to have if I can't trust you?

297
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:43,440
不知道，也许我是个闯祸星 也许你不该信任我
I don't know. I guess I'm just a jerk. Maybe you shouldn't trust me.

298
00:19:44,540 --> 00:19:45,780
这个当然也是方向之一
That's certainly one way to go.

299
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:49,140
我爸和我就选择了这个方向
That's the way my father went with me.

300
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:53,460
我曾经想，如果我有儿子 一定不会走这条路
I guess I hoped that when I had a son it would be different.

301
00:19:55,280 --> 00:19:56,340
我知道，老爸
I know, Dad.

302
00:19:58,340 --> 00:20:01,080
麦克，我想你已经忘了
Mike, you probably don't remember this, but...

303
00:20:01,266 --> 00:20:03,291
你三周大的时候…
when you were 3 weeks old...

304
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:10,220
我带你去看大都会的开垒
I took you to the Mets home opener.

305
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:14,780
抱着你摇啊摇
Cradled you in my arms.

306
00:20:15,347 --> 00:20:17,713
直到唐.克伦登…
Up comes Donn Clendenon.

307
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:21,700
在第12局将球击出左野外的 广告牌赢得比赛
Hits a shot off the left-field scoreboard to win it in the 12th.

308
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:24,620
我紧紧抱着你
I hugged you real tight...

309
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:26,540
高兴地跳着
jumping up and down.

310
00:20:26,780 --> 00:20:29,120
然后你就…
And you...

311
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:31,800
吐在你的棒球头盔里了
you threw up in your complimentary Mets batting helmet.

312
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:36,020
对不起，爸爸
I'm sorry, Dad.

313
00:20:37,680 --> 00:20:38,940
是我的错
It was my fault.

314
00:20:40,138 --> 00:20:43,198
我不该让你舔我手指上的啤酒
I never should've let you suck that beer off my finger.

315
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:48,720
不，爸爸，我说今晚对不起
No, Dad, I meant about tonight. I'm sorry.

316
00:20:53,280 --> 00:20:54,880
谢谢
Well, thank you.

317
00:20:57,560 --> 00:21:00,600
爸，我已经努力了，真的
You know, Dad, I try. I really try.

318
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,400
但有的时候…
But sometimes...

319
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:06,460
也不知道怎么回事 我就会做出点蠢事来
almost without warning, I just find myself doing something really stupid.

320
00:21:08,460 --> 00:21:10,340
就像是一种无法控制的冲动？
Sort of an uncontrollable impulse?

321
00:21:11,003 --> 00:21:11,992
没错
Yeah.

322
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:15,900
或者是这样，你知道自己 在做一件坏事…
Or is it more like you think you're doing something really stupid...

323
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:19,260
你估计一下免受惩罚的几率
and then you weigh your chances of getting away with it...

324
00:21:19,260 --> 00:21:21,480
如果几率大于10%，你就干
and if they're better than 10%, you go for it.

325
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:22,340
是啊
Yeah!

326
00:21:22,340 --> 00:21:23,540
所以你才会被禁闭两个月
That's why you're grounded for two months.

327
00:21:25,183 --> 00:21:26,309
是啊
Yeah.

328
00:21:28,860 --> 00:21:32,860
也许这话会让你好过点 我年轻时也干过荒唐的事
Well, if it makes you feel any better, I did some pretty lame-o things in my day.

329
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:35,300
-你？ -是的
- You? - Yeah.

330
00:21:35,660 --> 00:21:36,260
譬如呢？
Like what?

331
00:21:37,320 --> 00:21:38,520
记得我16岁的时候…
Like I remember when I was 16...

332
00:21:39,080 --> 00:21:41,740
我和几个哥们有天晚上开车乱转…
me and some buddies, we drove around town one night...

333
00:21:41,740 --> 00:21:42,780
向每个人露屁股 [Moon(月亮)：亦有朝某人露屁股之意]
mooning everybody.

334
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:46,560
我们甚至向市长夫人露屁股
We even mooned the mayor's wife.

335
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:48,660
真的？
You, Dad?

336
00:21:50,500 --> 00:21:53,020
我们因非法露体而被捕
Yeah, we got arrested for indecent exposure.

337
00:21:53,880 --> 00:21:55,220
不过还是把我们放了
Had to let us off though.

338
00:21:55,620 --> 00:21:57,940
市长夫人拒绝指认是哪个屁股
Mayor's wife refused to make an identification.

339
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:03,000
-真的？ -能不能别这种语气？
- You, Dad? - Will you stop saying that?

340
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:07,160
妈妈知道这事吗？
Does Mom know about this?

341
00:22:07,859 --> 00:22:08,340
这还用说
Are you kidding?

342
00:22:08,340 --> 00:22:10,580
你以为我们怎么认识的？
How do you think we met?

343
00:22:12,540 --> 00:22:14,140
好样的，老爸
All right, Dad.

344
00:22:17,420 --> 00:22:20,360
老爸，你现在还有做蠢事的冲动吗？
Hey, Dad, do you ever get the urge to do dumb stuff now?

345
00:22:23,980 --> 00:22:25,180
没有了，麦克
No, I don't, Mike.

346
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:28,560
成年人的区别就在于此
I think that's what being an adult is all about.

347
00:22:30,682 --> 00:22:31,671
Oh.

348
00:22:33,085 --> 00:22:34,882
好了，晚安，老爸
Well, all right. Good night, Dad.

349
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:36,500
晚安，儿子
Good night, son.

350
00:22:39,291 --> 00:22:40,280
Hey.

351
00:22:42,540 --> 00:22:44,120
再回来一下
Come back in here for a sec.

352
00:23:28,407 --> 00:23:35,404
三个孩子唱的是<月亮河> 英文“月亮”(moon）有“露屁股”之意

353
00:24:12,317 --> 00:24:13,306
谢谢观赏
